# KTP FastDL — keep server-side config OUT of the public docroot.
# Script: /usr/local/bin/ktp-fastdl-prune-configs.sh (canonical: KTPInfrastructure/scripts/).
#
# ktp-file-distributor lists /var/www/fastdl/dod as a target and watches *.cfg/*.ini, so any
# plugin config deployed to /home/dod/distribute is published publicly within ~7 seconds.
# The patterns cannot be narrowed -- the game servers need ac.ini and hltv_recorder.ini, and
# the distributor has no per-target filter. So the public copy is pruned on a short cycle.
#
# nginx also 404s these paths. This is the disk-layer half: it means a rebuilt or reverted
# nginx config cannot re-expose credentials that are no longer on disk.
*/10 * * * *   root  /usr/local/bin/ktp-fastdl-prune-configs.sh >> /var/log/ktp-fastdl-prune.log 2>&1
